{
  "_comment": "P4.D263 routes corpus for v4 app/api/v1/wardrobe/[itemId]/images/route.ts over the wardrobe-item-images tier-2 fixture. `@x` container ids name spec ids; a {ref} fileId is resolved against the baked fixture (the tier-2 rules). driver `http` = the real router (v5: a booted host, `oneshot`); `direct` = the generate leg with the provider mocked below both sides (v5: `generate_on_home` + the route's `render`). No HTTP request ever reaches a provider. P4.D275 (v4 `01a83539d`): GET `?action=save-targets` + the GET action dispatch (unknown / bare → 400 BEFORE the query), POST `?action=save-to-store`. A `{ref:{store:'@character'|'@archived'|'@project'|'@general'}}` names that entity's vault / official store / General; `{ref:{imageLink:<item>}}` the item's first `Wardrobe/images/` LINK id (not a `files.id`). `mountSql` plants the mount partition; `repeat` sends the request twice and records the second; `realStorage` un-mocks jest.setup's storage-manager stub on v4's side so `readImageBuffer` reads the picture's real mount blob, the bytes v5's `ProductionFileBytes` reads (M4). The dump grows the `photos/` links (their `extractedText` is the kept-image sidecar) and their blobs. The three listing `get_save_targets_*` rows run `direct` (v5: `resolve_home` + `save_targets_on_home` + the route's `render`): a BOOTED v5 host provisions the built-in Lantern Backgrounds + Quilltap Uploads stores into the fixture copy, which v4's unbooted oracle never has, and every enabled store is a save target. The GET dispatch's own rows (404, 400, unknown, bare) stay `http`.",
  "png": "iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAMAAAADCAIAAADZSiLoAAAACXBIWXMAAAPoAAAD6AG1e1JrAAAAEElEQVQImWNgZGKGIAYsLAADNgA3hQ4ykAAAAABJRU5ErkJggg==",
